    pass 3 phase 1: review follow-ups — landing time-boxed, event-scoped delete, raw_slice_replaced, lane-C landing non-fatal, runs row never lost
    
    Three critics (semantics, BigQuery platform, docs) read commit 136c77e; every confirmed finding is folded in.
    
    main.py: the four landing jobs take LAND_TIMEOUT_S (default 90 s) so a slow landing becomes raw_landing_failed inside the
    request instead of a killed request with the lease set; an event landing's delete-older is scoped to its own deal (two events
    of one entity in the same second share the slice key); land_raw() reports a replaced slice → raw_slice_replaced; write_run()
    retries without data_gaps at ERROR when new_deals_runs predates `deploy.sh tables`; docstrings corrected.
    deploy.sh: `deploy` applies `tables` first.
    sql/land_raw.sql: IFNULL(… IN UNNEST(…), FALSE) for in_scope (IN is NULL for a NULL pipeline; the column is NOT NULL);
    TO_JSON(…, stringify_wide_numbers => TRUE); owners with a NULL id skipped; raw_slice_replaced and labels_missing from @@row_count.
    sql/new_deals_weekly.sql: the spliced landing sits in BEGIN … EXCEPTION WHEN ERROR → raw_landing_failed, so the shadow contract
    holds for lane C too. sql/scheduled_query.sh: refuses a render without the landing and a dataset without `deploy.sh tables`;
    DRYRUN=1 fails on a real bq --dry_run error (both scripts).
    tests/test_main_offline.py: 18 tests — the ArrayQueryParameter object is pinned, strict replacement across two landings,
    labels-only failure, time-boxed jobs, runs row on an un-migrated table, event delete scope.
    docs: equality-check expectation corrected (first run on an empty warehouse names dedup_scope_batch_only), backfill slices
    excluded from the orphan probe, "28 of the 29 PROPS" for lane C, D5 emitted-vs-pending vocabulary, eleven hot-score inputs,
    timeline order, stale audit_tables text, schema comments.
    
    Recipe: .claude/skills/aider-scaffold/assets/recipes/a_raw_root.md
    Scaffolded-by: hand (no LLM key)
    
